'' An EXTERN's ALIAS is the name it links by, verbatim: case preserved, no '$', and
'' the same inside 'extern "C"' as outside it. Measured on fbc 1.20.0's -r output,
'' which emits 'extern int32 TheRealName;' for both spellings.
''
'' The unaliased one is the control: it keeps the uppercased, '$'-suffixed FreeBASIC
'' spelling, so this pins the alias path without claiming the ordinary one changed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/extern-alias-linkname.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: TheRealName
'' EXPECT-OUT: AlsoReal
'' EXPECT-OUT: PLAINONE$
'' EXPECT-NOT: ALIASED$
'' EXPECT-NOT: CALIASED$
